00:18:23.263 --> 00:18:24.731
And anything you find
without a warrant


00:18:24.763 --> 00:18:27.234
is fruit of the poison tree.


00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.969
I'm sorry, sis.


00:18:30.003 --> 00:18:31.971
Okay, we're legal.


00:18:32.003 --> 00:18:34.107
- Over there.
- All right!


00:18:34.139 --> 00:18:37.009
Susie, Cash, how y'all doin'?


00:18:40.446 --> 00:18:41.814
Move.


00:18:41.848 --> 00:18:43.648
Randy, want to start
at the bathroom?


00:18:43.683 --> 00:18:44.751
Sure.


00:18:44.783 --> 00:18:46.151
- You all right?
- Yeah.


00:18:46.185 --> 00:18:47.787
Why don't you go sit down
there, around the coffee table.


00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:48.989
I told you not
to let anyone in


00:18:49.022 --> 00:18:50.189
unless they showed
you a warrant.


00:18:50.255 --> 00:18:51.923
He showed me his
gun, all right?


00:18:51.957 --> 00:18:53.191
I didn't mean
that as a question.


00:18:53.193 --> 00:18:54.494
I said sit down.


00:19:01.868 --> 00:19:04.303
Ain't you got
somethin' to say?


00:19:05.105 --> 00:19:06.005
I didn't start this.


00:19:06.039 --> 00:19:08.205
You can stop it though.


00:19:08.207 --> 00:19:11.209
You want me to save
your dumb brother's ass?


00:19:11.211 --> 00:19:12.345
It's none of my business,
but I'd be worried


00:19:12.378 --> 00:19:14.481
about saving my own
ass right now, Cash.


00:19:14.513 --> 00:19:15.881
Is that right?


00:19:15.948 --> 00:19:17.548
Well, the cocaine
residue on the table alone


00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:18.784
is enough to violate you,


00:19:18.819 --> 00:19:20.551
send you back to
prison for two years.


00:19:20.553 --> 00:19:22.720
That is if your wife
flushed your whole stash,


00:19:22.722 --> 00:19:23.955
which I somehow doubt.


00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:26.859
Been peepin' through
keyholes, have you?


00:19:26.892 --> 00:19:28.794
Absolutely.


00:19:28.829 --> 00:19:30.964
Got a mirror in here.


00:19:32.299 --> 00:19:35.402
Looks like it was
used in a bakery.


00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.541
And a big ol' bag of
hillbilly heroin.


00:19:42.375 --> 00:19:44.411
Those are prescription!


00:19:45.911 --> 00:19:50.249
You got a prescription
for a thousands Percocet?


00:19:55.088 --> 00:19:57.023
He's got somethin' worth
a lot more than that.


00:19:58.257 --> 00:19:59.591
He knows somethin' that
will get him a deal


00:19:59.658 --> 00:20:00.994
and Bones one too.


00:20:02.261 --> 00:20:06.096
I don't want to be a party
to nobody gettin' ratted out!


00:20:06.098 --> 00:20:08.268
Be quiet, now, honey.


00:20:13.773 --> 00:20:16.008
What's that, Cash?


00:20:16.042 --> 00:20:17.877
I said I ain't sayin' nothin'


00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.278
until I get a deal in writin'.


00:20:20.346 --> 00:20:22.446
Oh, you've done
this before, huh?


00:20:22.448 --> 00:20:25.185
He's dones this
lots of times before.


00:20:25.217 --> 00:20:26.719
What do you say
we leave Cash here


00:20:26.753 --> 00:20:28.053
to think over his
limited options


00:20:28.087 --> 00:20:29.953
and take the brother
for drugs for now.


00:20:29.955 --> 00:20:32.524
I say we can do
whatever we want.


00:20:32.559 --> 00:20:33.893
All right.


00:20:33.926 --> 00:20:35.626
Bones shot that
boy in self-defense!


00:20:35.628 --> 00:20:37.126
That's a fact!


00:20:37.128 --> 00:20:38.531
Randy, man, listen for a second.


00:20:38.564 --> 00:20:39.532
Get off me!


00:20:39.565 --> 00:20:40.632
I'd say you're
on stronger ground


00:20:40.634 --> 00:20:42.800
that trying to talk your
husband into making a deal.


00:20:42.802 --> 00:20:44.137
Oh, is that right?


00:20:44.203 --> 00:20:46.138
Yeah, that's right.


00:20:48.206 --> 00:20:50.075
You hear that, Dick Four?


00:20:50.109 --> 00:20:55.215
I know where we're gettin'
outta this is if we make a deal.


00:20:57.984 --> 00:21:00.051
I gotta small wife, too, Cash.


00:21:00.086 --> 00:21:03.323
I find it best to
shut up and listen.


00:21:04.057 --> 00:21:05.258
Night-night.


00:21:09.294 --> 00:21:11.263
Okay, let me get this straight.


00:21:11.298 --> 00:21:13.099
You want a weekly salary.


00:21:13.132 --> 00:21:14.466
You want to be off probation,


00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.269
want to negotiate the
size of your bonus


00:21:16.302 --> 00:21:18.504
for this information before
you tell us what it is,


00:21:18.571 --> 00:21:22.574
and if you testify, you want
to be in witness protection?


00:21:22.608 --> 00:21:23.840
That's it?


00:21:23.842 --> 00:21:25.611
Mm-Hm.


00:21:25.645 --> 00:21:29.482
You do realise that's
a lot to ask, right?


00:21:29.515 --> 00:21:32.118
And even if you're John
Gotti, that's a lot to ask.


00:21:32.151 --> 00:21:35.654
Well, I got to a lot to offer.


00:21:35.687 --> 00:21:37.189
Who's John Gotti?


00:21:42.861 --> 00:21:44.263
All right.


00:21:44.296 --> 00:21:46.831
Entertain our guests
while I speak to my boss?


00:21:46.866 --> 00:21:47.768
Yeah.


00:21:48.702 --> 00:21:51.705
I'll tell 'em my fishin' story.


00:21:51.771 --> 00:21:54.773
So me an my cousin Fred, we
was out noodlin' one day...


00:21:54.808 --> 00:21:56.009
Eh, you got a phone I can use?


00:21:56.042 --> 00:21:58.542
Big guy, 'cause
he's from my mom's side.


00:21:58.544 --> 00:21:59.545
In private.


00:22:02.648 --> 00:22:05.185
Grabs it by lower lip,
pulls it outta the hole,


00:22:05.217 --> 00:22:08.386
wraps his legs
around the tail...


00:22:10.956 --> 00:22:12.525
62-pound flathead.


00:22:14.724 --> 00:22:14.827
He reached in with his hand?


00:22:14.860 --> 00:22:16.228
Yeah.


00:22:16.295 --> 00:22:17.129
They was noodlin',
you moron...


00:22:18.497 --> 00:22:19.165
Creekview.


00:22:19.198 --> 00:22:20.231
Who asked you?


00:22:20.299 --> 00:22:22.033
Susan Smith?


00:22:22.068 --> 00:22:23.067
Yeah?


00:22:23.069 --> 00:22:24.738
Y'all got a call.


00:22:39.584 --> 00:22:40.586
Yeah?


00:22:41.654 --> 00:22:43.523
It's me, your sister.


00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:46.526
- Somethin' wrong with the kids?
- No, no.


00:22:46.560 --> 00:22:50.329
Just someone from the Welfare
in West Virginia called.


00:22:50.362 --> 00:22:51.730
Shit.


00:22:51.764 --> 00:22:53.366
She was checkin' up on you.


00:22:53.398 --> 00:22:55.501
You're sure
she's from Welfare?


00:22:55.534 --> 00:22:58.772
Yeah, she knew your
case numbers and everything.


00:22:58.838 --> 00:23:00.572
All right, anything else?


00:23:00.606 --> 00:23:01.941
No, I just...


00:23:02.007 --> 00:23:04.107
thought you'd wanna know.


00:23:04.109 --> 00:23:05.108
Yeah, all right.


00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:06.513
Thanks.


00:23:06.545 --> 00:23:07.580
See ya later.


00:23:11.784 --> 00:23:15.120
Meet me in the parking lot
of the drive-thru at 7:00 a.m.


00:23:15.187 --> 00:23:16.119
7:00 a.m.?


00:23:16.121 --> 00:23:18.123
Why would I do that?


00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:20.191
To get your brother
a better deal.


00:23:20.225 --> 00:23:22.292
Keep your husband out of prison.


00:23:22.294 --> 00:23:25.931
Maybe get a little
somethin' for yourself, too.


00:23:25.965 --> 00:23:27.265
I don't want to talk
to Cash anymore.


00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.769
I wanna talk to the boss.


00:23:29.802 --> 00:23:31.204
When he asks you what
the call was about,


00:23:31.237 --> 00:23:33.305
say, "None of your
business, you don't own me."


00:23:33.372 --> 00:23:36.308
That way I'll know
you're comin'.


00:23:37.811 --> 00:23:40.480
You sicked the Welfare on me.


00:23:43.215 --> 00:23:44.317
There another option?


00:23:45.551 --> 00:23:47.986
Maybe ask for
something reasonable.


00:23:48.053 --> 00:23:50.389
His goddam boss said no.


00:23:53.225 --> 00:23:56.161
I did say you were
asking for too much, Cash.


00:23:56.228 --> 00:23:57.663
Well, if you want
to catch big fish,


00:23:57.730 --> 00:23:59.664
you gotta cut good bait.


00:23:59.666 --> 00:24:01.967
Did you really
tell them a fishing story?


00:24:02.001 --> 00:24:03.168
Yeah, I did.


00:24:03.235 --> 00:24:05.804
I didn't think it would
affect his mind, though.


00:24:05.838 --> 00:24:06.772
That's not funny, man.


00:24:06.805 --> 00:24:09.508
I got a lot to think about here.


00:24:11.510 --> 00:24:14.177
Who was bothering you
back there, anyway?


00:24:14.179 --> 00:24:16.416
None of your business.


00:24:18.818 --> 00:24:20.353
You don't own me.


00:24:26.359 --> 00:24:27.627
We done here?


00:24:29.294 --> 00:24:32.364
I could do with
a cup of coffee.


00:24:33.933 --> 00:24:34.935
Waitress!


00:25:09.901 --> 00:25:11.569
God damn her.


00:25:31.323 --> 00:25:32.024
There.


00:25:32.157 --> 00:25:35.227
This is for coming
to meet me today.


00:25:51.243 --> 00:25:52.445
Nice ride.


00:25:53.279 --> 00:25:54.513
Yeah?


00:25:55.881 --> 00:25:57.683
I inherited it from the
guy I replaced here.


00:25:57.716 --> 00:26:00.186
He just left for his new
assignment in Los Angeles.


00:26:00.219 --> 00:26:01.420
Lucky him.


00:26:02.621 --> 00:26:05.023
You're not a big
fan of Pikeville?


00:26:05.057 --> 00:26:06.526
I grew up in a town
about this size.


00:26:06.559 --> 00:26:09.061
Alls I know is every
time I fall down,


00:26:09.094 --> 00:26:10.628
I end up Rollin'
right back here.


00:26:10.696 --> 00:26:14.867
I figure that makes this
the bottom of the world.


00:26:14.900 --> 00:26:17.236
Well, your husband's
negotiated himself out of a deal


00:26:17.270 --> 00:26:19.972
that could get you
both outta here.


00:26:20.039 --> 00:26:22.541
Is he always this hard-headed
about getting what he wants?


00:26:22.574 --> 00:26:25.210
He won my heart, didn't he?


00:26:25.244 --> 00:26:27.645
And you keep callin'
him my husband.


00:26:27.647 --> 00:26:28.648
He's my ex.


00:26:29.615 --> 00:26:31.951
Yeah, but you live together.


00:26:31.984 --> 00:26:35.087
We live under the same roof.


00:26:35.120 --> 00:26:36.656
But we're not together.


00:26:37.889 --> 00:26:40.426
I can see he's not
smart enough for you.


00:26:40.458 --> 00:26:42.158
He's a dick four.


00:26:42.160 --> 00:26:43.795
What is a dick four, anyway?


00:26:48.767 --> 00:26:49.835
Well now.


00:26:49.903 --> 00:26:52.405
I just gotta keep that in
my little book of memories,


00:26:52.437 --> 00:26:54.340
mister hot shot FBI.


00:26:55.507 --> 00:26:59.578
I guess a shoulda seen
that one coming, huh?


00:27:02.514 --> 00:27:05.752
So what to you want
most outta life, Susan?


00:27:05.784 --> 00:27:07.319
Seriously, what would
turn your life around


00:27:07.352 --> 00:27:10.189
right now if it happened?


00:27:10.255 --> 00:27:11.123
You must think about it.


00:27:11.157 --> 00:27:12.524
I certainly do.


00:27:16.696 --> 00:27:17.696
Rehab.


00:27:21.033 --> 00:27:22.034
And money.


00:27:25.804 --> 00:27:27.039
Rehab and money.


00:27:34.679 --> 00:27:37.015
So you're a drug addict
who wants to get help,


00:27:37.050 --> 00:27:41.217
but you live with your
ex who's a coke dealer.


00:27:41.219 --> 00:27:43.388
I imagine that must be hard.


00:27:43.455 --> 00:27:44.624
I didn't say any of that.


00:27:44.657 --> 00:27:45.657
You did.


00:27:47.559 --> 00:27:51.130
Why don't I tell you
what I really want.


00:27:52.398 --> 00:27:54.533
I know what you want.


00:27:56.068 --> 00:28:00.540
And I know what's a federal
crime and what ain't.


00:28:04.577 --> 00:28:08.548
That's the
way the devil comes.


00:28:13.252 --> 00:28:15.754
He don't come to you as evil.


00:28:21.326 --> 00:28:23.863
He don't come to you on fire.


00:28:28.600 --> 00:28:32.004
He comes as everything
you ever wanted.


00:28:36.108 --> 00:28:38.845
He comes to you as you.


00:28:41.379 --> 00:28:44.447
That's my pappy right there.


00:28:44.449 --> 00:28:45.217
Hiram Grembly.


00:28:46.551 --> 00:28:51.457
And on the other side is
Cash's daddy, Amos G. Smith.


00:28:51.957 --> 00:28:53.559
Son of a bitch.


00:28:53.591 --> 00:28:55.093
So I remember you
saying when you fall down


00:28:55.127 --> 00:28:56.292
you always end up back here.


00:28:56.294 --> 00:28:57.461
Where did you fall down?


00:28:57.463 --> 00:28:59.963
You remember
everything I say, do you?


00:28:59.965 --> 00:29:01.600
Yeah, of course.


00:29:04.204 --> 00:29:05.469
Pittsburgh.


00:29:05.471 --> 00:29:08.741
Me and Cash, we lived in
Pittsburgh for a year.


00:29:08.773 --> 00:29:10.542
Why don't you tell me about
some of Cash's customers?


00:29:11.811 --> 00:29:15.114
You know, what they do for a
living, that kind of stuff.


00:29:15.147 --> 00:29:17.750
You mean what other
crimes do they commit


00:29:17.782 --> 00:29:20.086
that you can get
'em jammed up for?


00:29:20.119 --> 00:29:21.119
Exactly.


00:29:24.557 --> 00:29:28.461
Mark, I'd be takin'
a hell of a big risk.


00:29:28.494 --> 00:29:30.763
These people don't fuck around.


00:29:30.795 --> 00:29:33.398
They find out you're a snitch,
they burn down your house,


00:29:33.432 --> 00:29:36.068
and that is just a warnin'.


00:29:36.101 --> 00:29:37.736
You keep doin' it, they
will cut out your tongue


00:29:37.770 --> 00:29:39.171
and feed it to their dogs.


00:29:39.237 --> 00:29:42.475
That's why they'd be willing
to put you through rehab,


00:29:42.509 --> 00:29:44.911
send you and your kids
to a new state somewhere,


00:29:44.944 --> 00:29:48.281
give you a new
identity, a decent job.


00:29:49.648 --> 00:29:50.948
They do that?


00:29:50.983 --> 00:29:52.182
Yeah.


00:29:52.184 --> 00:29:53.853
They do it all the time.


00:29:54.987 --> 00:29:58.423
Look, if you help me bring
down this bank robber,


00:29:58.456 --> 00:30:01.260
I bet they pay you 10 grand.


00:30:01.292 --> 00:30:02.695
Yeah, 10 grand.


00:30:04.196 --> 00:30:06.031
I'm not judging you, Susan.


00:30:06.098 --> 00:30:07.499
I'm just saying, you've
never tried to make


00:30:07.532 --> 00:30:09.269
a clean break of it,
so don't give up hope.


00:30:09.301 --> 00:30:11.201
It's hope that's
fuckin' me up.


00:30:11.203 --> 00:30:12.838
I understand.


00:30:12.870 --> 00:30:14.205
Here.


00:30:14.273 --> 00:30:15.507
Take this for now.


00:30:15.541 --> 00:30:18.277
Just remember, big
risks pay big money.


00:30:18.311 --> 00:30:20.547
Small risks, small money.


00:30:21.813 --> 00:30:22.814
Okay?


00:32:16.494 --> 00:32:18.330
Pretty, ain't they?


00:32:20.965 --> 00:32:23.902
You wanna hold one of them guns?


00:32:24.669 --> 00:32:26.304
They feel like...


00:32:28.006 --> 00:32:29.007
power.


00:32:29.675 --> 00:32:30.909
You know?


00:32:39.185 --> 00:32:44.322
Just make sure you read the
papers the next few days, okay?


00:32:47.493 --> 00:32:50.196
Easy Street's just down yonder.


00:33:04.109 --> 00:33:04.943
Come on!


00:33:09.548 --> 00:33:10.483
Damn.


00:33:11.817 --> 00:33:14.384
You ain't started goin'
to church again, have you?


00:33:14.386 --> 00:33:15.888
Why?


00:33:15.955 --> 00:33:18.023
You wouldn't care if
I was being ordained.


00:33:18.057 --> 00:33:19.058
Am I right?


00:33:28.333 --> 00:33:29.000
Come on, Susan!


00:33:29.034 --> 00:33:30.468
You can't keep doing this to me.


00:33:30.503 --> 00:33:31.669
If you want me to
keep paying you,


00:33:31.704 --> 00:33:33.138
you have to give me something.


00:33:33.171 --> 00:33:33.972
Seriously.


00:33:34.005 --> 00:33:35.238
I've given you
hundreds of dollars,


00:33:35.240 --> 00:33:36.976
and you haven't given
me a goddam thing.


00:33:37.009 --> 00:33:38.676
I keep telling you.


00:33:38.709 --> 00:33:40.712
My life would be in danger.


00:33:40.746 --> 00:33:43.648
I know, but your life's
in danger now, isn't it?


00:33:47.352 --> 00:33:50.221
How long you think
you can keep this up?


00:33:50.255 --> 00:33:54.659
How long before you find
yourself in jail or dead?


00:33:54.693 --> 00:33:55.728
Then what are your
kids gonna do?


00:33:55.761 --> 00:33:56.926
How are they gonna live?


00:33:56.928 --> 00:33:58.095
You think the judge
will give 'em the cash,


00:33:58.163 --> 00:33:59.599
or you think they'll
wind up in foster care?


00:33:59.665 --> 00:34:00.499
You got a kid, huh?


00:34:00.532 --> 00:34:02.067
Yeah.


00:34:02.100 --> 00:34:03.034
Wife too?


00:34:03.869 --> 00:34:05.936
We're talkin'
about you, Susan.


00:34:06.003 --> 00:34:08.340
Tell me what she's like.


00:34:13.578 --> 00:34:14.781
Is she young?


00:34:17.616 --> 00:34:18.950
Is she pretty?


00:34:20.518 --> 00:34:22.854
Does she have a good body?


00:34:24.790 --> 00:34:28.791
She keeps herself fit,
if that's what you mean.


00:34:28.793 --> 00:34:31.460
Oh, she's too
high-class for me.


00:34:31.462 --> 00:34:32.130
Is that it?


00:34:32.197 --> 00:34:33.299
No.


00:34:33.364 --> 00:34:37.368
'Cause high class ain't a
always so good in a woman.


00:34:37.402 --> 00:34:39.103
If she won't suck your
dick at the movies,


00:34:39.138 --> 00:34:40.469
then what the hell
kinda good is she?


00:34:40.471 --> 00:34:42.374
Oh, come on.
Stop it.


00:34:43.643 --> 00:34:44.976
Cash may treat you
like a cheap whore,


00:34:45.043 --> 00:34:47.578
but that's no reason
to talk like one.


00:34:47.612 --> 00:34:48.581
Susan.


00:34:50.215 --> 00:34:52.315
You're the key to
everything I wanna do here.


00:34:52.317 --> 00:34:54.317
Do you understand that?


00:34:54.319 --> 00:34:57.255
To me, you're the most
important woman in this town.


00:34:57.288 --> 00:35:00.426
For God sake, learn
to act like it.


00:36:00.685 --> 00:36:02.552
He's name's Joe-Bea.


00:36:02.554 --> 00:36:04.557
My ex met him in prison.


00:36:05.556 --> 00:36:07.125
He lives with us.


00:36:08.893 --> 00:36:10.828
He has for four months.


00:36:10.862 --> 00:36:13.563
I didn't know how to tell you.


00:36:13.565 --> 00:36:14.567
I'm sorry.


00:36:20.239 --> 00:36:21.407
Outstanding.


00:36:23.842 --> 00:36:26.677
You've actually
seen the shotguns?


00:36:26.712 --> 00:36:28.681
Susan, this is amazing.


